Z||000003||Tigger||01-25-2001||10:30 PM||||I've heard rumors that the Jeep Willys concept is going to be NASA's next lunar/mars vehicle.      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"><P>Great times are ahead of us...<P>I was looking at an 1/18 scale model of an SUV looking vehicle made by a transportation design student from one of the leading art colleges in world.  Anyway, I kid you not, on the back corner of this thing was a flip up looking type of compartment and below it was the words "Caution Hot Coffee"<P>Great, can't wait to brew a fresh cup of joe on my drive to work every morning.      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"><P>------------------<BR>T-T-F-N, Ta Ta For Now!<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/tiggerblue3.gif"> <p>[This message has been edited by Tigger (edited 01-25-2001).]||||reg||4
Z||000004||Fformula88||01-25-2001||11:39 PM||||Can we all thank Ford's "new edge styling" for this trend?  I totally agree that auto styling is not looking all that hot.  But there are still some good ones...<P>I really like the styling of the Miata and the BMW Z3.  Both are great looking roadsters IMO!  A also like a lot of the exotics (Porsche 911, Ferari 360 Modena), but as for the more affordable cars... they just don't grab me.  There are two many harsh lines... the styling isn't clean anymore.<P>------------------<BR>John<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.geocities.com/formula2m6/FIEROSIG1.JPG">     <BR>1988 Fiero Formula<BR>1987 Fiero Sport Coupe *In rebuilding*<BR>1997 Ford Probe SE<BR>AOL IM: Fformula88||||reg||1
Z||000005||Homicidal||01-25-2001||11:54 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Fformula88:<BR><B>Can we all thank Ford's "new edge styling" for this trend?  I totally agree that auto styling is not looking all that hot.  But there are still some good ones...<P>I really like the styling of the Miata and the BMW Z3.  Both are great looking roadsters IMO!  A also like a lot of the exotics (Porsche 911, Ferari 360 Modena), but as for the more affordable cars... they just don't grab me.  There are two many harsh lines... the styling isn't clean anymore.<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Oh, the luxury and super sport cars are still gorgeous and are only getting nicer!<P>The Saleen S7, Porsche, Corvette Z26, Shelby Series 1, Morgan Aero 8, and the Mosler MT900 Twin Turbo are all just absolutely stunning.  But they are 2500-375K!!<P>It's the consumer cars that are these ghastley masses!<BR>||||reg||1
