Z||000009||2xsess||01-26-2001||08:14 AM||||I hate to say it but, I think Chrysler was on the right track with the Prowler, I think they all should go back and just slightly redefine the old body styles and rename them.  Me and one of the guys I work with were discussing new cars the other day. I think it's a shame that GM reintroduced the Monte Carlo, they should have left the name intact as what it was and thought up a new name for this new car. And as much as I liked the Impala SS , they should have changed the name when they brought out this new space designed body. As much as I dislike Chrysler products I do like the PT Cruiser, not so much because of it's body style but, because Chrysler showed cojones by producing it. No one else is thinking retro, they're all thinking, I want this one to go to space or something. Who knows!!!<P>I like my 85GT just fine, and I'm starting to feel like Sly in demonlition man, all these strange looking vehicles. <P>Well, I'll stop ranting now.<P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>AOL IM : Only2xsess<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/My_car_(large)sig_1.JPG">   <BR> <A HREF="http://kresgeus.homestead.com/FieroPage.html" TARGET=_blank>http://kresgeus.homestead.com/FieroPage.html</A> ||||reg||1
