Z||000025||StuGood||01-29-2001||12:58 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by jerpro:<BR><B>...it doesnt feel like you are driving at all! ...have to put a "baybysitter" aboard your vehicle because they think you can't drive   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif"> </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>jerpro, I agree.  You just echoed my biggest gripe about the newer vehicles.  I was driving a rental car recently (Monte Carlo I think?), and hated walking away with the (auto) lights on, not being able to put it in gear w/o depressing the brake pedal, etc.  I felt like the car had a mind of its own - I wasn't in control, like some kind of "B" horror movie.<P>Generally speaking, complex systems to take care of complex functions (e.g. - engine management) are a good idea. Complex systems to perform simple functions (turn lights on/ lock doors) are stupid, IMHO.<P>If I wanted to leave the driving to someone/ something else, I'd have taken a bus!  <P>Back to the subject at hand, yes, many vehicles seem to be getting uglier - Aztek being one example, IMO.  And Chrysler has some really bold "niche" vehicles - much better looking than most of AMC's "niche" efforts.  Now if Chrysler could just figure how to make more money...    ||||reg||14
Z||000026||MEC91Firebird||01-30-2001||10:45 PM||||Well, i cant say much for most of the run of the mill cars out there (if you dont want to spend $50,000+++), but i do belive that Pontiac is ahead of the pack, at least with there "normal" cars.  The GT and GTP Grand Prix's are killer looking cars!,  Especially the 5.7 V8 6-speeds they have been showing at the auto shows.  The Grand Am GT is nothing to scoff at either.  SSEi Bonnies are a great looking car to.  And the ABSOLUTE hottest car on the market today, (under $50G) has got to be the Ram-Air Trans Ams.  There is a car to be admired!!! Just imagine a FIERO that had the same styling cues as the Current Trans Am!!  That would be one hot car!!  (and woukld give the Vette a run for its money!).  <P>BTW, What do people think of the Ople Speedster as a "new" Fiero???  (as proposed by Road & Track?)||||reg||6
